From tru64-unix-managers  Sun Oct 17 07:50:18 1999
From: John Losey <JOHLOS () HBSI ! COM>
Date: Sun, 17 Oct 1999 07:50:18 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Drive Spin-down on an AlphaStation500
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079079016159

In my original question, I asked about disabling the drive spin down of the
RZ2DC-KBs in a Personal WorkStation 500au.

Thanks to Dr. Tom Blinn, Calvin Chung, Sean O'Connell, marc Baudoin,
Lawrence Philip, & doug for their help.

The simplest method was to open dxpower and uncheck "Spin down drives".  It
was also suggested I look in the pwrmgr section of /sysconfigtab and make
these changes:

pwrmgr:
        cpu_slowdown=0
        disk_spindown=0


Thank you all for your quick responses.  

John Losey
johlos@hbsi.com

