From: Kevin Jones <Kevin.Jones () compelsolve ! co ! uk>
Date: Thu, 14 Oct 1999 19:53:35 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: Installing sybase on T64u...
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079079016134

Sorry for the delay in summarising.

The answer is that it is not possible to put a raw data partition on the a
or c partition if they include the first sixteen blocks of the disk - this
is of course where the disklabel lives. A file system is aware of this
restriction and ignores the first sixteen blocks, a raw partition just sees
the partition as write protected.
Two main suggestions were made:
1. Make A partition very small and don't use it.
2. Make the A partition start at block 16 and write the label to partition
C.

Thanks Again

Kevin Jones

