   Tom Reu  (Tru64 UNIX Installation), and 
   alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com 
who all sent me answers. I had asked (excerpt): 

> ((...)) 
> 
> Reading the installation guide for 4.0F, I found table 3-3
> "Supported Disks for root File System" which lists RZ26
> disks as being supported but not RZ25.
> Does that mean I cannot install 4.0F to rz1 and rz2 (both RZ25),
> or is this just a way of telling me a single RZ25 will be
> too small ?

and all three of them agree that the disk type for the installation 
is not critical (so RZ25 are allowed) but the total space is, so 

   a single RZ25 will not be sufficient for Tru64 4.0F 

Quote from Tom Reu's answer: 
> Just for your info, our recommended minimums for file
> systems starting in V4.0d are:
>         root    128 MB
>         swap    128 MB
>         usr     700 MB
> 
> As you can see, it would be OK for root and swap to be on one
> RZ25. You could probably fit all of what you want for /usr on
> another, but it would not leave a lot for expansion/updates, etc. 

To me this signals I need /, /var, and some base swap on one RZ25 
and /usr on another, being cautious which subsets I really install. 

Thanks to all three of them (and any others whose answer might 
cross this summary)! 

Joerg Bruehe 

